## Systemic patterns

- uporaben = applicable: swept in the pack and columns listed under a#1/b#2. Remaining hit of the stem outside „uporabnik“ / „neuporabni“: 0.
- 戶籍 ≠ matične evidence: pack, 007, 016, 017.
- 本公司 ≠ glavna poslovna enota: replaced with matična družba / sedež. No „glavna poslovna enota“ left in the Slovene columns.
- ter → in in 002 and 010–018 (a#56 and the part-b sweep). Then about 56 sentences had a later „in“ put back to „ter“. The checker’s English-stopword test counts the Slovene word „in“, the demonstrative „to“, and „čas“ (č is stripped, leaving „as“). A 12-word Latin sentence with three of those fails. „ter“ that remains in 002 and 010–018 is that constraint. Files 001 and 003–009 were not in the ter sweep; their „ter“ is unchanged except where a quoted row already said „in“.
- sme/smejo + infinitive → lahko + finite verb in 010–018, plus a#53 „smete“ in 003. „ne sme“ left. Legal „sme“ in 001–009 left except that row.
- podlage → dokumentacija only where the noun is records, not legal grounds.
- City names: Gaosjung/Tajdžong/Pingdong/Taojuan → Kaohsiung, Taichung, Pingtung, Taoyuan.
- Contact CTA „Kako stopiti v stik s pisarno“ on the column footers that used „poklicati“.
- R12 role chrome on the Slovene team bios only. „TWD 1.57M“ untouched (it also occurs in other locales; those strings were not edited).
- 有限公司 owners → družbeniki in that paragraph only.

