## Reviewer got wrong (not applied)

- a#31: „ocene“ would make the UI read „17 ocene“. „17 ocen“ is the genitive plural the number requires.
- a#21: 大法官 are not „veliki sodniki Sodnega juana“. ACCEPTED’s „ustavni sodniki Sodnega sveta (大法官)“ is what was written. 司法院 is the Judicial Yuan and stays „Sodni juan“.
- a#70 / b#41: „500 000“ and moving „TWD“ after the amount fight R14 and the checker. Dot thousands and the existing TWD-first order stay.
- a#57 / a#65 / b#28: dropping the first person would contradict ACCEPTED („feminine narrator stays“) and the product fact that Wei Tseng is a woman. The feminine first person stays.
- b#11 „pot vložitve“: ACCEPTED overrides it with „pristojni organ / postopek“.
- b#33 „dva“: the checker counts the digit. „2 otroka“ stays; „edina“ still replaces „prizadeta“.
- „uporaben“ where it means useful or usable is correct Slovene and was not treated as the applicable-law false friend.
- „ne sme“ is a real prohibition. It was not rewritten as „ne lahko“.
- The 007 sentence that one word does not translate the whole of parental rights is in the English source. Only the 016 aside, which the English does not have, was removed.
